## Large programs: never lost, never stalled (Shay 2026-10-15, after the imm26 stop: a coordinator ended without a handoff and its agents sat orphaned ~90 min; work packages of 4-6 items hit the 200k meter before tests)
- **State lives in files:** every multi-part feature has a program ledger (`C:\KenshiTestRuns\programs\<name>.json` + a program md in `testing/`): work packages, state, owner agent, successor chain, outputs, last checkpoint. The coordinator updates it and HANDOFF "Right now" after EVERY agent report, not only at the context limit. `session-start.ps1` prints it.
- **Supervisor (hidden watchdog + coordinator heartbeat):** if a program has unfinished work packages and the coordinator heartbeat is stale > 10 min, a new coordinator session is launched automatically (rate-limited, alert after repeats); orphaned RUNNING agents (stale > 30 min) are marked STOPPED-CONTEXT and respawned fresh. A coordinator never ends a turn with todo/stopped packages (Stop hook).
- **Size work packages before spawning:** write a breakdown with token estimates first (`docs/WP_SIZING.md` section 2); one package = 1-3 related items or one phase (code | tests | patch/compose | native build | live validation), target <= 120k tokens, split anything touching more than 2 big files (> 60 KB). Never code + tests + live validation in one agent.
- **Big files are read through code maps:** `bash tools/automation/codemap.sh` (WSL) keeps `/root/imm26/codemap/<label>__<file>.txt` (name start end lines kind) for the large server PHP and STOBE C++ files; agents `grep -n funcname <map>` then `sed -n a,bp <file>`, never read a file > 60 KB whole; briefs name the functions to read. Regenerate a map after editing its file (`codemap.sh <file>`; `--check` lists stale maps).
- **Checkpoints and handoffs:** every milestone or ~40k tokens an agent regenerates its patch, compile-checks, updates its status `latest`, commits and updates its handoff, so a stop at 200k loses nothing. At the meter's warn level (before 200k): finish the edit, checkpoint, continue only if < 150k of work remains, else hand off (STOPPED-CONTEXT). Successors are fresh agents named wpA -> wpA2 -> wpA3 (the same work dir). Brief template: `docs/WP_SIZING.md` section 7.
- Details and the tooling that enforces this are recorded in `testing/AGENT_PROMPTS.md` (standard block) and `testing/HANDOFF.md`; if a rule here and a tool disagree, fix the tool.
<!-- LARGE-PROGRAMS-SLOT-END -->
- **Agent handoff guards (2026-10-15):** `agent-status.ps1` keeps `inflight\<name>` (created on RUNNING, deleted on DONE, kept on STOPPED-CONTEXT/FAILED) and writes `respawn\<name>.todo`. The Stop hook blocks on a STOPPED-CONTEXT/FAILED agent with no successor and counts every RUNNING status < 45 min old as in-flight work. `session-start.ps1` prints WAKER STATUS first, then ORPHANED / NO SUCCESSOR lines with the respawn text. Respawn a FRESH agent named <name>+suffix (2, b, -2) or the next number; never delete a stopped agent's marker before its successor exists; drop one on purpose with `agent-abandon.ps1 <name> "<why>"`. Usage: `testing/AGENT_PROMPTS.md` standard block.
- **Waker guard (restored 2026-10-15; `.claude/settings.json` Stop + PreToolUse hooks → `tools/automation/hooks/kenshi-waker-guard.ps1`):** the Stop hook blocks ending a turn while work is in flight (Kenshi running, game lock held, an inflight marker < 6 h old, or a fresh RUNNING agent) unless a waker is running; it blocks once on an idle 5090 with no fresh `kenshi-ctl.ps1 idle "<reason>"`. PreToolUse denies sleeps/wakeups > 120 s. Use `bash tools/automation/event-wait.sh [--batch <out>]` in the background (WSL) and restart it each time it wakes you; never the old `sleep 120` + health-check loop. Every new coordinator checks the "waker status" line from `session-start.ps1` first. If `.claude/settings.json` is rewritten, re-check that the guard entries are still there.

